=== wikino attachment get --help --json
{
  "args": [
    {
      "name": "attachment_id",
      "required": true,
      "variadic": false
    }
  ],
  "command": "wikino attachment get",
  "errors": "  1  Downloading from the signed URL failed (including expiry and interruption). Run the same command again. Or writing to the destination failed (permissions, disk space, and so on)\n  2  The ID is not a UUID, the destination directory does not exist, a file already exists at the destination (overwrite with `--clobber`), `--output -` is combined with `--json`, `--fields`, `--jq`, or `--clobber`, `--output -` is given while standard output is a terminal, or `--fields` has an unknown field\n  3  Not logged in, or the token is invalid or expired (401)\n  4  The token lacks the attachment:read scope (403)\n  5  The attachment does not exist or belongs to another space (404). Check the ID in `/attachments/{ID}` in the body and the space",
  "examples": "  # Save an attachment to the current directory with its original file name\n  wikino attachment get 01234567-89ab-cdef-0123-456789abcdef\n\n  # Pass the reference path from a body as is and save to the directory images/\n  wikino attachment get /attachments/01234567-89ab-cdef-0123-456789abcdef -O images/\n\n  # Save with a given file name, overwriting an existing file\n  wikino attachment get 01234567-89ab-cdef-0123-456789abcdef -O diagram.png --clobber\n\n  # Print the contents to standard output\n  wikino attachment get 01234567-89ab-cdef-0123-456789abcdef -O - > diagram.png",
  "flags": [
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Overwrite an existing file at the destination",
      "name": "clobber",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Destination file or directory (path; - for standard output)",
      "name": "output",
      "shorthand": "O",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "inherited_flags": [
    {
      "default": "[]",
      "description": "Comma-separated fields to print (e.g. number,title; applied to each item in lists)",
      "name": "fields",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "stringSlice"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Show help (as JSON when combined with --json)",
      "name": "help",
      "shorthand": "h",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Host url (defaults to the default host, or https://wikino.app)",
      "name": "host",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Filter results with a jq expr (applied after --fields)",
      "name": "jq",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Print results as JSON even on a TTY",
      "name": "json",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Member atname (to choose when the space has credentials for several members)",
      "name": "member",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Space identifier (space)",
      "name": "space",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "long": "Downloads the attachment with the given ID and saves it to a file.\nThe ID is the one in `/attachments/{ID}` in a body. You can also pass it with `/attachments/` left on.\n\nBy default, the file is saved to the current directory with its original file name.\nThe original file name is first cleaned into a name that points to a single file in the destination directory,\nfor example by removing path separators, control characters, and leading and trailing `.`.\n`--output` (`-O`) sets the destination file or directory, and `-` prints the contents to standard output.\nAn existing file is not overwritten and the command fails, unless `--clobber` is given.\n\nThe contents are downloaded from a short-lived signed URL returned by the API, without the token.",
  "output": "  Prints the following fields of the saved file.\n    id            ID of the attachment\n    path          Path of the saved file\n    filename      Original file name at upload. The saved file uses the cleaned name\n    content_type  Type of the file (e.g. image/png). null if not recorded\n    byte_size     Number of bytes saved\n  With `--output -`, only the contents are printed to standard output, without these fields.",
  "short": "Save an attachment",
  "subcommands": [],
  "usage": "wikino attachment get <attachment_id> [flags]"
}

=== wikino auth --help --json
{
  "args": [],
  "command": "wikino auth",
  "errors": "  A missing or unknown subcommand fails as a usage error (exit code 2).",
  "examples": "  # Log in by approving in the browser\n  wikino auth login my-space\n\n  # Over SSH, log in by entering a code in a browser on another device\n  wikino auth login my-space --device\n\n  # Log in with a personal access token from stdin\n  wikino auth login my-space --with-token < token.txt\n\n  # Check saved credentials and token scopes\n  wikino auth status",
  "flags": [],
  "inherited_flags": [
    {
      "default": "[]",
      "description": "Comma-separated fields to print (e.g. number,title; applied to each item in lists)",
      "name": "fields",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "stringSlice"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Show help (as JSON when combined with --json)",
      "name": "help",
      "shorthand": "h",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Host url (defaults to the default host, or https://wikino.app)",
      "name": "host",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Filter results with a jq expr (applied after --fields)",
      "name": "jq",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Print results as JSON even on a TTY",
      "name": "json",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Member atname (to choose when the space has credentials for several members)",
      "name": "member",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Space identifier (space)",
      "name": "space",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "long": "Log in to Wikino spaces and manage saved credentials.\n\nCredentials are saved per combination of host, space, and member.\nTokens are saved in the OS keychain, or in a 0600 file in the config directory (`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wikino/`, or `~/.config/wikino/` if unset) where the keychain is unavailable.\nSet `WIKINO_TOKEN_STORE=file` to always save to a file.\n\nCommands decide the host, space, and member in this order.\n  Host: `--host` → `WIKINO_HOST` → default host → https://wikino.app\n  Space: `--space` → `WIKINO_SPACE` → default space → the only space with credentials\n  Member: `--member` → `WIKINO_MEMBER` → the space's default member → the only member with credentials in the space\n\nA token in `WIKINO_TOKEN` takes precedence over saved credentials, and nothing is written to disk.\nIn that case, give the space with `--space` or `WIKINO_SPACE`, and do not give `--member` or `WIKINO_MEMBER`.",
  "output": "  See the help of each subcommand.",
  "short": "Manage login and credentials",
  "subcommands": [
    {
      "command": "wikino auth login",
      "name": "login",
      "short": "Log in to a space"
    },
    {
      "command": "wikino auth logout",
      "name": "logout",
      "short": "Remove saved credentials"
    },
    {
      "command": "wikino auth status",
      "name": "status",
      "short": "Check credentials and tokens"
    },
    {
      "command": "wikino auth switch",
      "name": "switch",
      "short": "Switch the default space and member"
    }
  ],
  "usage": "wikino auth <command>"
}

=== wikino auth login --help --json
{
  "args": [
    {
      "name": "space",
      "required": false,
      "variadic": false
    }
  ],
  "command": "wikino auth login",
  "errors": "  2  No space is given, `--member` is given, `--scopes` is empty or has an unknown scope, `--with-token` is combined with `--scopes` or `--device`, or the token on stdin is empty or malformed\n  3  Approval was denied on the authorization page (authorization_denied), the authorization response did not match the request, the authorization server returned an error, or it does not support device authorization (oauth_error), or the token is invalid or expired (401)\n  5  The token does not belong to the space (404). Give the identifier of the space that issued the token\n  1  Approval did not happen within 5 minutes or before the device authorization code expired (login_timeout), the authorization server's response could not be read (response_error), the connection failed, or saving the token or configuration (or restoring after a failed save) failed\n  Nothing is saved if API validation fails.\n  If only removing the token from its previous store fails, login succeeds with a warning, and the removal can be retried with login or logout.",
  "examples": "  # Log in by approving in the browser\n  wikino auth login my-space\n\n  # Over SSH, log in by entering a code in a browser on another device\n  wikino auth login my-space --device\n\n  # Request only the read and draft scopes\n  wikino auth login my-space --scopes page:read,draft_page:read,draft_page:write\n\n  # Log in with a personal access token saved in a file\n  wikino auth login my-space --with-token < token.txt\n\n  # Log in to a development server\n  wikino auth login my-space --host http://localhost:4000",
  "flags": [
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Log in with device authorization (approve by entering a code in a browser on another device)",
      "name": "device",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "[]",
      "description": "Scopes to request (comma-separated). Defaults to all scopes that can be granted to a token",
      "name": "scopes",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "stringSlice"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Read a personal access token from stdin",
      "name": "with-token",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    }
  ],
  "inherited_flags": [
    {
      "default": "[]",
      "description": "Comma-separated fields to print (e.g. number,title; applied to each item in lists)",
      "name": "fields",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "stringSlice"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Show help (as JSON when combined with --json)",
      "name": "help",
      "shorthand": "h",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Host url (defaults to the default host, or https://wikino.app)",
      "name": "host",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Filter results with a jq expr (applied after --fields)",
      "name": "jq",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Print results as JSON even on a TTY",
      "name": "json",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Member atname (to choose when the space has credentials for several members)",
      "name": "member",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Space identifier (space)",
      "name": "space",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "long": "Log in to a space and save the credentials.\n\nBy default, Wikino's authorization page opens in the browser and a token is obtained after approval (OAuth).\nThe URL of the authorization page is also printed to stderr; open it if the browser does not open.\nApproval is awaited for up to 5 minutes.\n\nWhen connected over SSH, when there is no display, or when launching the browser or listening on a port fails, device authorization is used instead.\nWith `--device`, device authorization is always used.\nWith device authorization, a verification URL and a code are printed to stderr; open the URL in a browser on your own device, enter the code, and approve.\nApproval is awaited until the code expires (10 minutes on Wikino).\n\nBy default all scopes that can be granted to a token are requested, and the granted scopes can be chosen on the authorization page.\nTo request fewer scopes, give `--scopes`.\nOAuth access tokens are refreshed automatically shortly before they expire, before calling the API.\n\nWith `--with-token`, a personal access token issued in the space settings is read from stdin.\n\nEither way, the token is saved only after the API confirms it works in the space; nothing is saved otherwise.\nWhen logging in with the browser, a token that was not saved is revoked on the server.\nThe member is determined by the token, so do not give `--member`.\n\nIf there is no default yet, the logged-in combination becomes the default.\nIf the space has no default member yet, the logged-in member becomes the space's default.\nLogging in again as the same member replaces the saved token.",
  "output": "  Prints the saved credentials.\n    host           Host URL\n    space          Space identifier\n    member         Member (id, atname, name)\n    token_store    Where the token is saved (keyring, file)\n    default        Whether this is the default combination\n    space_default  Whether this is the space's default member\n    scopes         Scopes granted when logging in with the browser (not printed with `--with-token`)\n  The authorization page URL, the device authorization's verification URL and code, and a warning when the keychain is unavailable and the token is saved to a file, are printed to stderr.",
  "short": "Log in to a space",
  "subcommands": [],
  "usage": "wikino auth login [<space>] [flags]"
}

=== wikino auth logout --help --json
{
  "args": [
    {
      "name": "space",
      "required": false,
      "variadic": false
    }
  ],
  "command": "wikino auth logout",
  "errors": "  2  The space or member cannot be decided (candidates are shown in the hint)\n  3  There are no credentials for the given space or member\n  1  The token or configuration could not be removed. Credentials remain in the configuration so logout can be retried.",
  "examples": "  # Remove the credentials for the space my-space\n  wikino auth logout my-space\n\n  # Remove the credentials for another member of the same space\n  wikino auth logout my-space --member bot",
  "flags": [],
  "inherited_flags": [
