=== wikino draft create --help --json
{
  "args": [
    {
      "name": "page_number",
      "required": false,
      "variadic": false
    }
  ],
  "command": "wikino draft create",
  "errors": "  1  Network failure or server error (5xx). The draft may have been created.\n     Check with `wikino draft get <page_number>` for an existing page, or `wikino draft list` for a new page, before sending again\n  2  Neither or both of a page number and `--topic` are given, the page number or `--topic` is not a positive integer, both `--body` and `--body-file` are given,\n     the body file cannot be read or is not UTF-8, `--fields` has an unknown field, or `--dry-run` is combined with `--fields`\n  3  Not logged in, or the token is invalid or expired (401)\n  4  The token lacks the draft_page:write scope, lacks page:write for a new page, or lacks page:read for checking the linked pages of the body (403)\n  5  You cannot create drafts in the page or topic, or the page does not exist when checking the linked pages of the body (404)\n  6  The page already has a draft of yours (409). Read the current draft with `wikino draft get <page_number>` and update it with `wikino draft update <page_number>`\n  7  Invalid input such as the title, or the page or topic does not exist or cannot be seen (422). Fix the field shown in the error.\n     If the page or topic number is the problem, check it with `wikino page list` or `wikino topic list`",
  "examples": "  # Create a draft of page 12 with its current content\n  wikino draft create 12\n\n  # Create a draft of page 12 with the content of a file as the body\n  wikino draft create 12 --body-file minutes.md\n\n  # Create a draft of a new page titled \"Minutes\" in topic 3, and print only the page number and version\n  wikino draft create --topic 3 --title 'Minutes' --body '# Minutes' --fields page_number,etag\n\n  # Check the request that would be sent and where the wikilinks in the body point (without sending it)\n  wikino draft create 12 --body-file minutes.md --dry-run",
  "flags": [
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Body text (Markdown) as a string",
      "name": "body",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Read the body from the file at path (`-` reads from standard input)",
      "name": "body-file",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Print the requests that would be sent without sending them",
      "name": "dry-run",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "The draft's title. For an existing page, defaults to the page's current title. The page title rules (up to 200 characters, without `/`, `\\`, `:`, or control characters, and without a leading or trailing space) are checked when publishing",
      "name": "title",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "The number of the topic to create a draft of a new page in. Cannot be combined with a page number",
      "name": "topic",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "inherited_flags": [
    {
      "default": "[]",
      "description": "Comma-separated fields to print (e.g. number,title; applied to each item in lists)",
      "name": "fields",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "stringSlice"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Show help (as JSON when combined with --json)",
      "name": "help",
      "shorthand": "h",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Host url (defaults to the default host, or https://wikino.app)",
      "name": "host",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Filter results with a jq expr (applied after --fields)",
      "name": "jq",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Print results as JSON even on a TTY",
      "name": "json",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Member atname (to choose when the space has credentials for several members)",
      "name": "member",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Space identifier (space)",
      "name": "space",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "long": "Creates a draft for rewriting a page without publishing it.\nOne revision of the draft's history is created at the same time.\n\nTo create a draft of an existing page, pass the page number as the argument.\nIf `--title` and the body are omitted, the page's current title and body become the draft.\nYou cannot create one when the page already has a draft of yours.\nRead the current draft with `wikino draft get` and update it with `wikino draft update`.\n\nTo create a draft of a new page, specify the topic with `--topic` instead of a page number.\nAs when creating one in the web UI, an unpublished page without a title or body is created, along with its draft.\nOmitting `--title` gives a draft without a title, and omitting the body gives a draft with an empty body.\n`page_number` in the output is the number of the new page.\n\nPass the body with `--body` or `--body-file`; `--body-file -` reads it from standard input.\nThe body is sent as given, including trailing newlines.\nTitle rules (such as no duplicates within a topic) are checked when the draft is published.\n\nWhen a wikilink in the body points to a page that does not exist, the linked page is created as an unpublished page.\nWhen a body is given, the command checks where the wikilinks in the body point before creating, and if any linked pages will be created, it lists them on standard error after creating.\nThe list is an estimate made just before creating; if other users create or delete pages in between, it can differ from the actual result.\nTo check for unintended linked pages beforehand, use `--dry-run`.\n\nCreating a draft of a new page is not idempotent.\nWhen the result is unknown (such as after a network failure), check whether it was created with `wikino draft list` before sending again.\n\nCreating a draft of a new page requires the page:write scope on the token in addition to draft_page:write.\nChecking the linked pages of the body requires the page:read scope.\nCreating a draft of a page in a private topic also requires the topic:read scope.",
  "output": "  Prints the created draft with the same fields as `wikino draft get` (including `etag`).\n  To update it next, pass `etag` to `--if-match` of `wikino draft update`.\n  The human-readable output omits the body and prints a completion line to standard error.\n  If wikilinks in the body are estimated to have created linked pages, lists them on standard error, also with JSON output.\n  With `--dry-run`, prints the request that would be sent and where the wikilinks in the body point as `{\"dry_run\": true, \"requests\": [...], \"wikilinks\": [...]}` without sending the create request.\n  See the help of `wikino page create` for the fields of `wikilinks`.\n  The requests that fetch the existing page to check the linked pages and that check the linked pages (both reads) are sent even with `--dry-run`.\n  `--dry-run` cannot be combined with `--fields`.",
  "short": "Create a draft",
  "subcommands": [],
  "usage": "wikino draft create [<page_number>] [flags]"
}

=== wikino draft delete --help --json
{
  "args": [
    {
      "name": "page_number",
      "required": true,
      "variadic": false
    }
  ],
  "command": "wikino draft delete",
  "errors": "  2  The page number is not a positive integer, neither or both of `--if-match` and `--force` are given, `--if-match` is empty or `*`, `--fields` has an unknown field, or `--dry-run` is combined with `--fields`\n  3  Not logged in, or the token is invalid or expired (401)\n  4  The token lacks the draft_page:delete scope (403)\n  5  You have no draft of the page, the page does not exist or is in the trash, or the page is in a private topic you cannot see (404).\n     If you get 5 when deleting again, the draft has already been deleted\n  6  The draft has been updated since you read it (412). Check the current content with `wikino draft get`, and delete again with the new version if it is fine to delete\n  9  Confirmation by the user is required because `--yes` is not given, or the confirmation was declined in a terminal",
  "examples": "  # Read the draft of page 12 and check its version, then ask for confirmation to delete it\n  wikino draft get 12 --md\n  wikino draft delete 12 --if-match '\"d41d8cd9\"'\n\n  # Delete without asking, after getting the user's approval\n  wikino draft delete 12 --if-match '\"d41d8cd9\"' --yes\n\n  # Check the request (without sending)\n  wikino draft delete 12 --if-match '\"d41d8cd9\"' --dry-run",
  "flags": [
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Print the requests that would be sent without sending them",
      "name": "dry-run",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Overwrite the latest version, fetched just before, without checking the version you read",
      "name": "force",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Write only if the version is still the one you read (etag from the output of `get`)",
      "name": "if-match",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Run without asking for the user's confirmation",
      "name": "yes",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    }
  ],
  "inherited_flags": [
    {
      "default": "[]",
      "description": "Comma-separated fields to print (e.g. number,title; applied to each item in lists)",
      "name": "fields",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "stringSlice"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Show help (as JSON when combined with --json)",
      "name": "help",
      "shorthand": "h",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Host url (defaults to the default host, or https://wikino.app)",
      "name": "host",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Filter results with a jq expr (applied after --fields)",
      "name": "jq",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Print results as JSON even on a TTY",
      "name": "json",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Member atname (to choose when the space has credentials for several members)",
      "name": "member",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Space identifier (space)",
      "name": "space",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "long": "Deletes your draft of the page with the given page number, together with its revisions.\nThe deleted draft and revisions cannot be restored.\nThe page itself is not deleted, and the content of the published page does not change.\n\nPass the version you read in `--if-match`.\nThe version is `etag` in the output of `wikino draft get`.\nIf the draft has been updated since you read it (including automatic saves in the web editor), the command fails with exit code 6 without deleting it.\nWith `--force`, the command does not check the version and deletes the latest version it has just fetched.\n\nBecause this cannot be undone, the command asks for confirmation before deleting unless `--yes` is given.\nWhen run from a terminal, it shows the draft and the number of revisions to delete and asks.\nOtherwise (when run from an agent or a script), it does not send the delete request; it prints what will happen (`changes`) and the command to run after approval (`confirm_command`) as JSON on standard output, and exits with code 9.\nShow `changes` to the user, and run `confirm_command` as is after getting approval.\n`confirm_command` contains the version fetched for the confirmation in `--if-match`.\n\nDeleting requires the draft_page:delete scope on the token.\nThis scope also includes reading the draft and its revisions for the confirmation and for `--force`.\nDeleting drafts of pages in private topics also requires the topic:read scope.",
  "output": "  After deleting, prints `{\"page_number\": 12, \"deleted\": true}` as JSON.\n  The human-readable output prints nothing on standard output and prints a completion line to standard error.\n  Without `--yes` and outside a terminal, prints `{\"status\": \"confirmation_required\", \"changes\": [...], \"confirm_command\": \"...\"}` without deleting, and exits with code 9.\n  With `--dry-run`, prints the request as `{\"dry_run\": true, \"requests\": [...]}` without sending the delete request. It does not ask for confirmation.\n  Fetching the draft with `--force` (a read) is sent even with `--dry-run`.\n  `--dry-run` cannot be combined with `--fields`.",
  "short": "Delete a draft",
  "subcommands": [],
  "usage": "wikino draft delete <page_number> [flags]"
}

