=== wikino draft update --help --json
{
  "args": [
    {
      "name": "page_number",
      "required": true,
      "variadic": false
    }
  ],
  "command": "wikino draft update",
  "errors": "  2  The page number is not a positive integer, none of `--title`, `--body`, `--body-file`, `--md-file`, and `--edits` is given, flags that cannot be combined are combined,\n     neither or both of `--if-match` and `--force` are given (except with `--md-file` and `--edits`), `--if-match` is empty or `*`, a file cannot be read or is not UTF-8,\n     `wikino_number` in `--md-file` differs from the page number or `wikino_etag` is missing, the JSON in `--edits` has the wrong shape, `--fields` has an unknown field, or `--dry-run` is combined with `--fields`\n  3  Not logged in, or the token is invalid or expired (401)\n  4  The token lacks the draft_page:write scope, or the page:read scope for checking the links in the body (403)\n  5  You have no draft of the page, the page does not exist or is in the trash, or the page is in a private topic you cannot see (404).\n     Check the number with `wikino draft list`, and create a draft with `wikino draft create` if there is none\n  6  The draft has been updated since you read it (412). Get the latest content and version with `wikino draft get`, apply your changes, and update again.\n     With `--md-file`, apply your changes to a file written again with `wikino draft get --md`\n  7  The input is invalid, such as a title or body that is too long (422).\n     `old_str` in `--edits` does not match the current body or matches more than one place (422). The hint shows which edit, and the message shows the number of matches.\n     Check the current body with `wikino draft get --md` and send the whole `edits` again",
  "examples": "  # Get the version of the draft of page 12, then update its body with the content of a file\n  wikino draft get 12 --jq .etag\n  wikino draft update 12 --body-file body.md --if-match '\"d41d8cd9\"'\n\n  # Change only the title of the draft of page 12\n  wikino draft update 12 --title 'Meeting notes' --if-match '\"d41d8cd9\"'\n\n  # Write the draft of page 12 to a file, edit it, and write it back\n  wikino draft get 12 --md > draft.md\n  wikino draft update 12 --md-file draft.md\n\n  # Find and replace part of the body of the draft of page 12\n  echo '{\"edits\": [{\"old_str\": \"- [ ] Share the notes\", \"new_str\": \"- [x] Share the notes\"}]}' | wikino draft update 12 --edits -\n\n  # Check the request and where the wikilinks in the body point (without sending)\n  wikino draft update 12 --body-file body.md --if-match '\"d41d8cd9\"' --dry-run",
  "flags": [
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Body text (Markdown) as a string",
      "name": "body",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Read the body from the file at path (`-` reads from standard input)",
      "name": "body-file",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Print the requests that would be sent without sending them",
      "name": "dry-run",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Read find-and-replace edits as JSON (path) and replace part of the body (`-` reads from standard input)",
      "name": "edits",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Overwrite the latest version, fetched just before, without checking the version you read",
      "name": "force",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Write only if the version is still the one you read (etag from the output of `get`)",
      "name": "if-match",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Write back a page file (path) written by --md, using the version and title in its frontmatter (`-` reads from standard input)",
      "name": "md-file",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "New title of the draft. The page title rules (up to 200 characters, without `/`, `\\`, `:`, or control characters, and without a leading or trailing space) are checked when publishing",
      "name": "title",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "inherited_flags": [
    {
      "default": "[]",
      "description": "Comma-separated fields to print (e.g. number,title; applied to each item in lists)",
      "name": "fields",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "stringSlice"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Show help (as JSON when combined with --json)",
      "name": "help",
      "shorthand": "h",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Host url (defaults to the default host, or https://wikino.app)",
      "name": "host",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Filter results with a jq expr (applied after --fields)",
      "name": "jq",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Print results as JSON even on a TTY",
      "name": "json",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Member atname (to choose when the space has credentials for several members)",
      "name": "member",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Space identifier (space)",
      "name": "space",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "long": "Updates the title and body of your draft of the page with the given page number.\nOnly the given fields are updated; the others are left unchanged.\nThe page is not published, and the content of the published page does not change.\nEach update also creates one draft revision (none if it is the same as the previous revision).\n\nChoose one of three ways to pass the body, depending on the size of the change.\n\n- `--body` or `--body-file`: pass the whole body, including the parts you do not change. `--body-file -` reads the body from standard input. The body is sent as given, including trailing newlines\n- `--md-file`: write back a page file written by `wikino draft get --md` and edited. The command uses `wikino_etag` in the frontmatter as the version and `wikino_title` as the title, and sends the rest, without the keys starting with `wikino_`, as the body\n- `--edits`: find and replace part of the body. Reads JSON shaped like `{\"edits\": [{\"old_str\": \"...\", \"new_str\": \"...\", \"replace_all\": false}]}` from a file or standard input (`-`)\n\n`--md-file` and `--edits` follow the same rules as in `wikino page update`.\nWith `--md-file`, a file whose `wikino_number` differs from the page number or that has no `wikino_etag` is rejected, and the title is unchanged if `wikino_title` is missing.\n`--edits` cannot change the title.\n\nPass the version you read in `--if-match`.\nThe version is `etag` in the output of `wikino draft get`.\nThe version also changes when the web editor saves automatically, so if the draft has been updated since you read it, the command fails with exit code 6 without overwriting it.\nWith `--force`, the command does not check the version and overwrites the latest version it has just fetched.\nThis can discard what is being written in the web editor, so use it only when it is fine to overwrite without reading.\nWith `--md-file`, the version is read from the file, so do not pass `--if-match` or `--force`.\nWith `--edits`, `--if-match` is optional.\n\nWhen a wikilink in the body points to a page that does not exist, the linked page is created as an unpublished page.\nBefore writing the body, the command checks where its wikilinks point (with `--edits`, it checks the links in each `new_str`), and if any linked pages will be created, lists them on standard error after the update.\nThe list is an estimate made just before the update and can differ from the actual result if other users create or delete pages in between.\nUse `--dry-run` to check for unintended linked pages first.\n\nTitle rules (such as no duplicate titles in a topic) are checked when the draft is published.\n\nChecking where the links in the body point requires the page:read scope on the token in addition to draft_page:write.\nUpdating drafts of pages in private topics also requires the topic:read scope.",
  "output": "  Prints the updated draft with the same fields as `wikino draft get` (including `etag`).\n  `etag` is the version after the update; pass it to `--if-match` for the next update.\n  The human-readable output omits the body and prints a completion line to standard error.\n  If wikilinks in the body are expected to have created linked pages, lists them on standard error, even with JSON output.\n  With `--dry-run`, prints the request and where the wikilinks in the body point as `{\"dry_run\": true, \"requests\": [...], \"wikilinks\": [...]}` without sending the update.\n  See the help for `wikino page update` for the fields in `wikilinks`.\n  Fetching the draft when writing the body or with `--force`, and checking the links (both reads), are sent even with `--dry-run`.\n  `--dry-run` cannot be combined with `--fields`.",
  "short": "Update a draft",
  "subcommands": [],
  "usage": "wikino draft update <page_number> [flags]"
}

