  "long": "Lists the pages that link to the specified page with wiki links, most recently updated first.\nThese are the same pages as the list of backlinks shown below the page on the web.\n\nOnly links in each page's published body count; links only in a draft are not included.\nPages in the trash and pages in private topics you cannot see are not included.\n\nTo find the pages this page links to instead, use `wikino page links`.\n\nThe output format and paging are the same as `wikino page list`.\nThe list does not include page bodies; it includes an excerpt of the beginning of the body (`excerpt`) instead.",
  "output": "  Like `wikino page list`, prints `{\"items\": [...], \"next_cursor\": ...}`.\n  See the help of `wikino page list` for the fields of each page.\n  `excerpt` is not part of the API response; the CLI builds it from the body. `body` is printed only when included in `--fields`.\n  With `--all`, prints JSON Lines where each line is one item, without `next_cursor`.\n  When no pages link to the page, returns an empty list with exit code 0.",
  "short": "List the pages that link to a page",
  "subcommands": [],
  "usage": "wikino page backlinks <page_number> [flags]"
}

=== wikino page create --help --json
{
  "args": [],
  "command": "wikino page create",
  "errors": "  1  Network failure or server error (5xx). The page may have been created, so check with `wikino page list --topic <number> --title <title>` before sending again\n  2  `--topic` or `--title` is missing, neither or both of `--body` and `--body-file` are given, `--topic` is not a positive integer,\n     the body file cannot be read or is not UTF-8, `--fields` has an unknown field, or `--dry-run` is combined with `--fields`\n  3  Not logged in, or the token is invalid or expired (401)\n  4  The token lacks the page:write scope (403)\n  5  You cannot create pages in the topic (404)\n  7  The title does not follow the rules in `--title`, a page with the same title exists in the topic, or the topic does not exist or cannot be seen (422).\n     For a duplicate, find the existing page with `wikino page list --topic <number> --title <title>` and use `wikino page update` to change its content",
  "examples": "  # Create a page titled \"Minutes\" in topic 3\n  wikino page create --topic 3 --title 'Minutes' --body '# Minutes'\n\n  # Create a page with the content of a file as the body\n  wikino page create --topic 3 --title 'Minutes' --body-file minutes.md\n\n  # Read the body from standard input and print only the number and version of the created page\n  cat minutes.md | wikino page create --topic 3 --title 'Minutes' --body-file - --fields number,etag\n\n  # Check the request that would be sent and where the wikilinks in the body point (without sending it)\n  wikino page create --topic 3 --title 'Minutes' --body-file minutes.md --dry-run",
  "flags": [
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Body text (Markdown) as a string",
      "name": "body",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Read the body from the file at path (`-` reads from standard input)",
      "name": "body-file",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Print the requests that would be sent without sending them",
      "name": "dry-run",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Page title. Required. Up to 200 characters, without `/`, `\\`, `:`, or control characters, and without a leading or trailing space",
      "name": "title",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Topic number to create the page in. Required",
      "name": "topic",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "inherited_flags": [
    {
      "default": "[]",
      "description": "Comma-separated fields to print (e.g. number,title; applied to each item in lists)",
      "name": "fields",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "stringSlice"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Show help (as JSON when combined with --json)",
      "name": "help",
      "shorthand": "h",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Host url (defaults to the default host, or https://wikino.app)",
      "name": "host",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Filter results with a jq expr (applied after --fields)",
      "name": "jq",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Print results as JSON even on a TTY",
      "name": "json",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Member atname (to choose when the space has credentials for several members)",
      "name": "member",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Space identifier (space)",
      "name": "space",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "long": "Creates and publishes a page with a title and a body in the topic with the given topic number.\n\nPass the body with either `--body` or `--body-file`.\nTo create an empty page, say so explicitly with `--body ''`.\n`--body-file -` reads the body from standard input.\nThe body is sent as given, including trailing newlines.\n\nIf an unpublished page with the same title and no body exists (such as a page created by a wikilink), the body is written to that page and it is published instead of creating a new page.\nIn that case, `number` in the output is the number of that page.\n\nWhen a wikilink in the body points to a page that does not exist, the linked page is created as an unpublished page.\nBefore creating, the command checks where the wikilinks in the body point, and if any linked pages will be created, it lists them on standard error after creating.\nThe list is an estimate made just before creating; if other users create or delete pages in between, it can differ from the actual result.\nTo check for unintended linked pages beforehand, use `--dry-run`.\n\nCreating a page is not idempotent.\nWhen the result is unknown (such as after a network failure), check whether the page was created with `wikino page list --topic <number> --title <title>` before sending again.\n\nTo change the content of an existing page, use `wikino page update`.\nCreating a page in a private topic requires the topic:read scope on the token in addition to page:write.",
  "output": "  Prints the created page with the same fields as `wikino page get` (including `etag`).\n  To update it next, pass `etag` to `--if-match` of `wikino page update`.\n  The human-readable output omits the body and prints a completion line to standard error.\n  If wikilinks in the body are estimated to have created linked pages, lists them on standard error, also with JSON output.\n  With `--dry-run`, prints the request that would be sent and where the wikilinks in the body point as `{\"dry_run\": true, \"requests\": [...], \"wikilinks\": [...]}` without sending the create request.\n  Each element of `wikilinks` has the wikilink text (`text`), the name of the linked topic (`topic_name`), the page title (`page_title`), the resolution (`resolution`), and the existing page (`page`).\n  `resolution` is one of: an existing page (`existing_page`), a page that writing creates as unpublished (`new_page`), or a topic that does not exist or cannot be seen, so the text is not a link (`topic_not_found`).\n  The request that checks the linked pages (a read) is sent even with `--dry-run`.\n  `--dry-run` cannot be combined with `--fields`.",
  "short": "Create a page",
  "subcommands": [],
  "usage": "wikino page create [flags]"
}

=== wikino page get --help --json
{
  "args": [
    {
      "name": "page_number",
      "required": true,
      "variadic": false
    }
  ],
  "command": "wikino page get",
