    }
  ],
  "long": "Shows the page with the given page number, including its body.\nUnpublished pages are shown too.\n\nWith `--md`, prints a page file in the Wikino file format (Markdown with frontmatter).\n`--md` suits reading bodies because line breaks and quotes are not escaped.\nFor a large page, write it to a file with `--md` and read only the parts you need.\n\n`etag` in the output is the version of the page.\nWhen updating the page, pass the version you read to `--if-match`.",
  "output": "  Prints the page with the fields of `wikino page list` (without excerpt, with body) plus the following.\n    etag  Version of the page (the ETag response header). Pass it to `--if-match` of update commands\n  With `--md`, prints a page file in the Wikino file format instead of JSON.\n  The frontmatter keys starting with `wikino_` hold the number, title, version, topic number, status, update time, and URL,\n  followed by the body as is. When the body itself starts with frontmatter, the keys are added to that block.",
  "short": "Show a page",
  "subcommands": [],
  "usage": "wikino page get <page_number> [flags]"
}

