  ],
  "long": "Lists the pages of the space, most recently updated first.\nPages in the trash are not included.\n\nBy default, lists only published pages.\nWith `--status unpublished` or `--status all`, also lists pages not yet published, such as pages created automatically by wiki links.\nUnpublished pages are included only when referenced by wiki links from published pages in topics you can see or from your own drafts.\nUnpublished pages without those links are not included.\n\nThe list does not include page bodies; it includes an excerpt of the beginning of the body (`excerpt`) instead.\nUse `wikino page get` to read a body.\nWhen you need bodies in the list, include `body` in `--fields`.\n\nBy default, fetches only one page with the API's default size (20).\nWhen there is a next page, prints how to fetch it to standard error.\nWith `--all`, fetches every item and the output becomes JSON Lines (see Output).\n\nPages in private topics are included only when the token has the topic:read scope and the member can see the topic.",
  "output": "  Prints `{\"items\": [...], \"next_cursor\": ...}` with these fields per page.\n    id            Page ID\n    number        Page number. Pass it to `wikino page get` and other commands\n    title         Title. null for a page without a title\n    status        Publication status (published, unpublished)\n    topic_number  Number of the topic the page belongs to\n    topic_name    Name of the topic the page belongs to. Use it in wiki links to pages in other topics (`[[Topic name/Title]]`)\n    modified_at   When the content was last updated (RFC 3339)\n    url           URL to open the page on the web. Use it to cite the page\n    excerpt       Excerpt of the beginning of the body: the first 80 characters with line breaks collapsed into spaces,\n                  ending with \"…\" when truncated. Not part of the API response; the CLI builds it from the body\n    body          Body (Markdown). Omitted by default; printed only when included in `--fields`\n  `next_cursor` is the cursor of the next page, or null when there is none.\n  With `--all`, prints JSON Lines where each line is one item, without `next_cursor`.\n  When no pages match, returns an empty list with exit code 0.",
  "short": "List pages",
  "subcommands": [],
  "usage": "wikino page list [flags]"
}

