      "name": "space",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "long": "Lists the pages whose title or body contains the keywords, most recently updated first.\nSearches only within the token's space.\nPages in the trash are not included.\n\nYou can quote the keywords as one argument or list them separated by spaces.\nMultiple keywords separated by whitespace (including full-width spaces) match only pages containing all of them (AND search).\nEach keyword may appear in either the title or the body.\nMatching is by substring and case-insensitive.\nYou can specify up to 10 keywords.\n\nBy default, searches only published pages.\nWith `--status all`, also searches pages not yet published.\n\nThe output format and paging are the same as `wikino page list`.\nThe list does not include page bodies; it includes an excerpt of the beginning of the body (`excerpt`) instead.\nUse `wikino page get` to read a body.\n\nPages in private topics are included only when the token has the topic:read scope and the member can see the topic.",
  "output": "  Like `wikino page list`, prints `{\"items\": [...], \"next_cursor\": ...}`.\n  See the help of `wikino page list` for the fields of each page.\n  `excerpt` is not part of the API response; the CLI builds it from the body. `body` is printed only when included in `--fields`.\n  With `--all`, prints JSON Lines where each line is one item, without `next_cursor`.\n  When no pages match, returns an empty list with exit code 0.\n  In human-readable output, prints a hint on loosening the search to standard error.",
  "short": "Search pages by keywords",
  "subcommands": [],
  "usage": "wikino page search <query>... [flags]"
}

=== wikino page update --help --json
{
  "args": [
    {
      "name": "page_number",
      "required": true,
      "variadic": false
    }
  ],
  "command": "wikino page update",
  "errors": "  2  The page number is not a positive integer, none of `--title`, `--body`, `--body-file`, `--md-file`, and `--edits` is given, flags that cannot be combined are combined,\n     neither or both of `--if-match` and `--force` are given (except with `--md-file` and `--edits`), `--if-match` is empty or `*`, a file cannot be read or is not UTF-8,\n     `wikino_number` in `--md-file` differs from the page number or `wikino_etag` is missing, the JSON in `--edits` has the wrong shape, `--fields` has an unknown field, or `--dry-run` is combined with `--fields`\n  3  Not logged in, or the token is invalid or expired (401)\n  4  The token lacks the page:write scope (403)\n  5  The page does not exist, is in the trash, or cannot be updated (404). Check the number with `wikino page list`\n  6  The page has been updated since you read it (412). Get the latest content and version with `wikino page get`, apply your changes, and update again.\n     With `--md-file`, apply your changes to a file written again with `wikino page get --md`\n  7  The title does not follow the rules in `--title`, a page with the same title exists in the topic, or an untitled unpublished page was updated without `--title` (422).\n     `old_str` in `--edits` does not match the current body or matches more than one place (422). The hint shows which edit, and the message shows the number of matches.\n     Check the current body with `wikino page get --md` and send the whole `edits` again",
  "examples": "  # Get the version of page 12, then update its body with the content of a file\n  wikino page get 12 --jq .etag\n  wikino page update 12 --body-file body.md --if-match '\"d41d8cd9\"'\n\n  # Change only the title of page 12\n  wikino page update 12 --title 'Minutes of the weekly meeting' --if-match '\"d41d8cd9\"'\n\n  # Write page 12 to a file, edit it, and write it back\n  wikino page get 12 --md > page.md\n  wikino page update 12 --md-file page.md\n\n  # Find and replace part of the body of page 12\n  echo '{\"edits\": [{\"old_str\": \"- [ ] Share the minutes\", \"new_str\": \"- [x] Share the minutes\"}]}' | wikino page update 12 --edits -\n\n  # Overwrite the latest version without checking the version\n  wikino page update 12 --body-file body.md --force\n\n  # Check the request that would be sent and where the wikilinks in the body point (without sending it)\n  wikino page update 12 --body-file body.md --if-match '\"d41d8cd9\"' --dry-run",
  "flags": [
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Body text (Markdown) as a string",
      "name": "body",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Read the body from the file at path (`-` reads from standard input)",
      "name": "body-file",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Print the requests that would be sent without sending them",
      "name": "dry-run",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Read find-and-replace edits as JSON (path) and replace part of the body (`-` reads from standard input)",
      "name": "edits",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Overwrite the latest version, fetched just before, without checking the version you read",
      "name": "force",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Write only if the version is still the one you read (etag from the output of `get`)",
      "name": "if-match",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Write back a page file (path) written by --md, using the version and title in its frontmatter (`-` reads from standard input)",
      "name": "md-file",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "New title. Up to 200 characters, without `/`, `\\`, `:`, or control characters, and without a leading or trailing space",
      "name": "title",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "inherited_flags": [
    {
      "default": "[]",
      "description": "Comma-separated fields to print (e.g. number,title; applied to each item in lists)",
      "name": "fields",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "stringSlice"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Show help (as JSON when combined with --json)",
      "name": "help",
      "shorthand": "h",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Host url (defaults to the default host, or https://wikino.app)",
      "name": "host",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Filter results with a jq expr (applied after --fields)",
      "name": "jq",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Print results as JSON even on a TTY",
      "name": "json",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Member atname (to choose when the space has credentials for several members)",
      "name": "member",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "description": "Space identifier (space)",
      "name": "space",
      "shorthand": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "long": "Updates the title and body of the page with the given page number.\nOnly the given fields are updated; the others are left unchanged.\n\nChoose one of three ways to pass the body, depending on the size of the change.\n\n- `--body` or `--body-file`: pass the whole body, including the parts you do not change. `--body-file -` reads the body from standard input. The body is sent as given, including trailing newlines\n- `--md-file`: write back a page file written by `wikino page get --md` and edited. The command uses `wikino_etag` in the frontmatter as the version and `wikino_title` as the title, and sends the rest, without the keys starting with `wikino_`, as the body\n- `--edits`: find and replace part of the body. Reads JSON shaped like `{\"edits\": [{\"old_str\": \"...\", \"new_str\": \"...\", \"replace_all\": false}]}` from a file or standard input (`-`)\n\nPassing a page file to `--body-file` makes the frontmatter part of the body.\nPass page files with `--md-file`.\n\nA page file for `--md-file` is read as follows.\nA file whose `wikino_number` differs from the page number argument, and a file without `wikino_etag`, are rejected.\nWithout `wikino_title`, the title is not changed.\nOther `wikino_` keys (status, modification time, URL, and so on) are read-only and ignored even if edited.\nThe body's own frontmatter (keys that do not start with `wikino_`) is kept as part of the body.\n\nEach edit in `--edits` replaces, in array order, the places matching `old_str` in the body after the earlier edits are applied with `new_str`.\n`old_str` must match the body exactly, including case, spaces, and line breaks.\nAn edit with `replace_all` set to `false` (the default) fails unless it matches exactly one place, and then no edit is applied.\n`--edits` cannot change the title.\n\nTo update, pass the version you read to `--if-match`.\nThe version is `etag` in the output of `wikino page get`.\nIf the page has been updated since you read it, the command fails with exit code 6 without overwriting.\nWith `--force`, the version is not checked and the latest version, fetched just before, is overwritten.\nThis can discard other people's changes, so use it only when overwriting without reading is acceptable.\nWith `--md-file`, the version is read from the file, so do not add `--if-match` or `--force`.\nWith `--edits`, `--if-match` can be omitted.\nThat `old_str` matches the current body itself confirms that the edit is based on the body you read.\nWith `--if-match`, the edits are applied only to the body of the version you read.\n\nWhen a wikilink in the body points to a page that does not exist, the linked page is created as an unpublished page.\nBefore writing the body, the command checks where its wikilinks point (with `--edits`, the wikilinks in each `new_str`), and if any linked pages will be created, it lists them on standard error after updating.\nThe list is an estimate made just before updating; if other users create or delete pages in between, it can differ from the actual result.\nTo check for unintended linked pages beforehand, use `--dry-run`.\n\nUpdating a page that is not yet published publishes it.\nIf the title and body are the same as now, nothing is updated and the current page is printed.\n\nUpdating a page in a private topic requires the topic:read scope on the token in addition to page:write.",
  "output": "  Prints the updated page with the same fields as `wikino page get` (including `etag`).\n  `etag` is the version after the update; pass it to `--if-match` to update again.\n  The human-readable output omits the body and prints a completion line to standard error.\n  If wikilinks in the body are estimated to have created linked pages, lists them on standard error, also with JSON output.\n  With `--dry-run`, prints the request that would be sent and where the wikilinks in the body point as `{\"dry_run\": true, \"requests\": [...], \"wikilinks\": [...]}` without sending the update request.\n  Each element of `wikilinks` has the wikilink text (`text`), the name of the linked topic (`topic_name`), the page title (`page_title`), the resolution (`resolution`), and the existing page (`page`).\n  `resolution` is one of: an existing page (`existing_page`), a page that writing creates as unpublished (`new_page`), or a topic that does not exist or cannot be seen, so the text is not a link (`topic_not_found`).\n  The requests that fetch the page (when writing the body or with `--force`) and check the linked pages (reads) are sent even with `--dry-run`.\n  `--dry-run` cannot be combined with `--fields`.",
  "short": "Update a page",
  "subcommands": [],
  "usage": "wikino page update <page_number> [flags]"
}

=== wikino skill --help --json
{
  "args": [],
  "command": "wikino skill",
  "errors": "  A missing or unknown subcommand fails as a usage error (exit code 2).",
